  "summary": "The committee examined how regulatory sandboxes help financial firms test new products and engage with the Financial Conduct Authority (FCA). Desmond McNamara said Zilch used the process to launch regulated credit sooner, while Benjamin Cave said Aveni valued contact with the regulator but wanted more sustained expert guidance and better testing data, especially for AI. The witnesses differed on how much extra guidance firms need: Cave called for clearer discussion of uncertain cases, while McNamara warned that detailed new rules could limit innovation and said firms must remain responsible for customer outcomes. They also discussed who benefits, mentoring, competition, costs and whether the name “sandbox” still fits.",
